WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.310
- Welcome back, I'm hanging
out with Idina Menzel.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.143
Give it up!

00:00:03.143 --> 00:00:05.372
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.130
So the New York Times calls our next guest

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.870
Magic's Best Kept Secret,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.540
which is saying a lot
because, well, it's magic.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.860
He's collaborated with David,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.180
See what I did there?
(chuckling)

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.610
He's collaborated with
David Blaine for 15 years

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.220
to create some of his most
mind bending illusions.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.230
And now he has his own off-Broadway show

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.320
called David Blaine Presents
Asi Wind's Inner Circle.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.919
Everybody say hi to Asi Wind.

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:28.500
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.453
Meet Idina.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.350
So, I love magic, so I'm
very, very, very excited.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.580
Okay, so David Blaine says

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.960
that you're his favorite magician.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.940
That's a lot of weight
to carry; that's awesome.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.773
- I know!

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.490
But so it happens he's
my favorite magician too.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.340
I mean, he pushed the limits of magic

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.120
over the last 15, 20
years and became my hero.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.116
And now I'm honored that
he's presenting my show.

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:52.113
It's amazing.

00:00:52.113 --> 00:00:53.310
- Yeah, it's so cool.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.143
I love that you both have

00:00:54.143 --> 00:00:55.380
such a fond respect of each other.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.213
That's so cool.

00:00:56.213 --> 00:00:57.046
So what are you showing us today?

00:00:57.046 --> 00:00:58.320
I see cards.
- Let's warm up.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.250
Let's warm up.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.083
- Let's warm up.

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.164
- Exactly right. So can
I ask you this question?

00:01:02.164 --> 00:01:05.040
If you can just name a
favorite card or random card.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.873
- [Kelly] Queen of hearts.

00:01:05.873 --> 00:01:06.706
- The which?

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:07.539
- Queen of hearts.

00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:08.372
- Okay, I do this.
(card deck slapping)

00:01:08.372 --> 00:01:09.930
- Okay.
(fingers snapping)

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.730
- Reach into my pocket.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.783
- No way.

00:01:13.849 --> 00:01:15.060
- Go for it.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.012
- I will slap you.

00:01:17.012 --> 00:01:18.390
(audience and Idina laughing)

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.912
- No way.
(gasps)

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.347
(screams)

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:25.430
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:26.358 --> 00:01:28.929
(Asi laughing)

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:29.762
- That's amazing.

00:01:29.762 --> 00:01:31.890
- How would you have done
that with slight of hand

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.020
or like I don't even
understand how that, what?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.700
- Should we try something crazier?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.750
- 100 percent.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.490
- Okay, let's do it.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.510
I don't assume.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.795
Do you don't have bills on
you or purse or something?

00:01:41.795 --> 00:01:43.109
I need like a -
- Do we look like strippers?

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:44.790
(audience laughing)

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.860
No, I don't, but I can
ask someone for money.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.780
Wouldn't it be amazing if
I just pulled some out?

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.613
- [Asi] I would be shocked.

00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:50.446
- Can I have some money, Chris?

00:01:50.446 --> 00:01:51.600
Do you got any money?
- [Chris] I got money.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.440
- Come on, Chris.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.570
- Like at least four, five, six bills.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.403
Something like, yeah.

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:56.236
Yeah, put it here if you don't mind.

00:01:56.236 --> 00:01:58.260
- Okay, just like this?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.130
- Okay.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.099
- So here's what I'd like you to do.

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:01.182
- Thanks, Chris.

00:02:01.182 --> 00:02:02.790
- I would like you,

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.873
first of all, how many
bills do we have here?

00:02:04.873 --> 00:02:06.360
- [Kelly] All right, Chris.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.350
- [Asi] Wow. Look at that!

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.780
- It's a nice variety,
it's a really nice variety.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.627
Can you please, Idina,

00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:14.130
please put your finger right there.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:15.960
And Kelly name a number
between one and five.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.793
Just say it out.
(fingers snapping)

00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:17.626
- Four!
- Four.

00:02:17.626 --> 00:02:19.830
Okay. So take the fourth bill down.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:20.760
One.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.593
- [Idina] One.

00:02:21.593 --> 00:02:22.517
- [Asi] Two
- [Idina] Two.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.470
Three.
- [Asi] Three.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.660
Four.
- [Asi] And the fourth one,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.920
I don't wanna see it, just fold it.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.480
Yeah, take the fourth bill.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.313
Yeah, take it out.

00:02:28.313 --> 00:02:29.146
- [Idina] Take it out?

00:02:29.146 --> 00:02:30.090
- [Asi] And fold it a few times.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.100
The rest of them we'll put aside.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.970
You remind me.
- Okay.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.474
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:02:34.474 --> 00:02:35.310
- [Chris] Hey, hey!

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.297
- I know, I know, I get it.

00:02:36.297 --> 00:02:37.393
- [Idina] That's a lot of money in there.

00:02:37.393 --> 00:02:38.430
- It's how you get paid. I got it.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.350
- Kelly, as I drop cards onto the table,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.910
you call the word stop.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.810
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:43.680
- Okay. I'll do it again.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.210
- Okay.
- Okay means stop?

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.200
Or we'll do it again?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.460
- Oh! Oh! I'll say stop.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.990
- Okay so -
- Stop!

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.690
- [Asi] Look, if you say
add two more, three more,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.523
I will do it.

00:02:52.523 --> 00:02:53.460
Unless you like it here.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.293
- I like it there.

00:02:54.293 --> 00:02:55.980
- No more? Not one more,
two more, three more,

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.180
five more, whatever you want?

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.080
- No, I want that one.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:58.950
- Say the word stop.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.090
- [Kelly] Stop!
- [Asi] That's good?

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:00.923
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:02.430
- [Asi] And one last
time say the word stop.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.263
- [Kelly] Stop.

00:03:03.263 --> 00:03:05.880
- [Kelly] So all of these,
because you said stop, go away.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.630
Between those four piles,
one, two, three, and four,

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.300
I want you to turn one
over and you turn one over.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.133
Face down.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.143
- [Kelly] Just turn one over, like this?

00:03:14.143 --> 00:03:14.976
- [Asi] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:15.809
The whole pile.

00:03:15.809 --> 00:03:17.100
- [Kelly] Oh, okay!

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:17.933
- [Asi] You can do the whole pile.

00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:18.766
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:18.766 --> 00:03:19.599
- [Asi] And you, the whole pile.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.510
So now we have cards going
face up and face down.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.130
- So excited! Okay.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.069
- [Asi] Hold on, it's getting better.

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.250
(Idina laughing)

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.910
So can you push these into these? Push.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.080
- [Kelly] Push them.
- [Asi] Push it like that.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.810
So now you can see we need,
don't square anything,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.640
but you can see cards going
different ways, right?

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.260
- [Idina] Yes.
- [Asi] Different ways.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.820
Between these two piles.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.800
Should we turn this over or these over?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.940
It's up to you.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:39.773
- Turn those over.

00:03:39.773 --> 00:03:41.933
- So all of these will be
turned this way, right?

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:42.766
- Okay.

00:03:42.766 --> 00:03:44.313
- Can you push these into these?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.830
- [Kelly] I just like how
you say it with your accent.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.663
That's so cool.

00:03:47.663 --> 00:03:49.133
- I fake it, just it looks more authentic.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:49.966
(all laughing)

00:03:49.966 --> 00:03:51.791
It's really cool.

00:03:51.791 --> 00:03:52.624
- I like it.

00:03:52.624 --> 00:03:54.150
- Usually it's American.
- I like it.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.230
- Okay.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.063
Last time.

00:03:56.063 --> 00:03:57.480
This one or this one?

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.313
- [Kelly] That one.

00:03:58.313 --> 00:03:59.252
- Interesting.
- Okay?

00:03:59.252 --> 00:04:00.085
(Idina chuckles)

00:04:00.085 --> 00:04:00.918
- What does it say about Kelly?

00:04:00.918 --> 00:04:02.940
It's like handwriting analysis.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.320
- I went with less is more.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.761
- Yeah, it's interesting.
I like that approach.

00:04:05.761 --> 00:04:06.594
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:08.490
- [Asi] Can you push these into these?

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.323
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:09.323 --> 00:04:10.170
- [Asi] Push these into these.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.360
- [Asi] You agree that's a mess

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.320
- [Kelly] Yeah, chaotic, chaos.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.400
- I want you to look close

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.020
as I just square the deck.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.910
Just square the deck like this.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.743
- [Kelly] Don't know what's happening.

00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:19.980
- [Asi] And look what's gonna happen.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.813
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:20.813 --> 00:04:23.820
- [Asi] I'm gonna make
every single card in here

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.930
go face down.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.730
Meaning I'll fix every card.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.563
- Okay.

00:04:27.563 --> 00:04:28.396
- Ready?
- How?

00:04:28.396 --> 00:04:29.744
- Watch.

00:04:29.744 --> 00:04:31.260
(card deck flipping)

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.243
That's it. Every card will, hold on,

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.050
cause I see they're face up still.

00:04:37.019 --> 00:04:37.890
(hand clapping)

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:38.948
That's it.

00:04:38.948 --> 00:04:39.781
(Idina laughing)

00:04:39.781 --> 00:04:40.614
- What?

00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:42.060
- All of them are now face down.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.160
- But I see the white.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.603
- Really? Let me see.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.883
- [Kelly] Wait, what do you
mean? Wait, what do you mean?

00:04:51.302 --> 00:04:52.320
Wait, what do you mean?

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.250
- No, what I meant to say

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.441
is that most of them are face down.

00:04:55.441 --> 00:04:57.390
(audience laughing)

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.510
- [Asi] It's what? It's
six, seven, eight cards?!

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.343
Kelly, Kelly.

00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:02.176
- Totally.

00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:03.009
- This is where I get nervous.

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:04.260
Like, did this come out wrong,

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.552
and you want us to start over?

00:05:05.552 --> 00:05:07.080
- Let me tell you something.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.970
In today's economy, that's pretty good.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:09.803
- It's true.

00:05:09.803 --> 00:05:10.710
- It's true.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.253
- But hold on.

00:05:12.253 --> 00:05:14.850
You shuffled them, face up, face down.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.560
And I asked you all
along the way, how many,

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.130
and how many piles, and I
asked you to bring some bills.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.340
These are your bills,
and you chose this bill.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.840
You know this bill is unique.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.280
Can I show you something?

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.480
This bill is unique because
it's a one of a kind.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.180
This dollar bill does
not exist anywhere else,

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.084
because you see the serial
number is one of a kind.

00:05:37.084 --> 00:05:37.917
(Kelly and Idina gasp)

00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:38.750
So look at the number.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:39.583
Can you read it out loud, Kelly?

00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:40.416
- What?!

00:05:40.416 --> 00:05:41.370
- [Asi] Seven. Read it, seven.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.203
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:05:42.203 --> 00:05:45.930
- [Asi and Kelly] Seven,
two, one, three, nine, five,

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.610
three, four.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.903
- [Asi] Three and four.

00:05:50.052 --> 00:05:50.885
- Oh my god.

00:05:50.885 --> 00:05:53.698
(audience cheering)

00:05:53.698 --> 00:05:55.713
- Oh my god.
- Thank you so much.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.455
- That was incredible.

00:06:00.162 --> 00:06:02.263
I can't stop, that was so mindblowing.

00:06:02.263 --> 00:06:03.300
I love magic.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.371
Oh my god.

00:06:04.371 --> 00:06:06.026
Asi Wind, everybody, give it up.

00:06:06.026 --> 00:06:07.435
(audience cheering)

00:06:07.435 --> 00:06:09.852
Wow. If you're New York area,

00:06:11.081 --> 00:06:13.034
you can see him live in person.

00:06:13.034 --> 00:06:14.638
You will want to do this.

00:06:14.638 --> 00:06:16.514
That was incredible.

00:06:16.514 --> 00:06:18.963
His new show is called
Asi Wind's Inner Circle.

